# Backend (Python)

Managed with **[Poetry](https://python-poetry.org/)** — `pyproject.toml` + `poetry.lock` are the source of truth.

| Concern | Choice |
|--------|--------|
| Runtime | Python ≥ 3.10 |
| API | FastAPI + Pydantic (async for I/O-bound work) |
| Tests | pytest (+ pytest-asyncio for async routes) |
| CLI | Rich |
| Imaging | NiBabel (NIfTI); pybids for layout |

## Structure & quality

- Packages by concern: `api/`, `services/`, `bids/`, `pipelines/`, `models/`.
- Type hints on public APIs; long jobs via task IDs — never block HTTP on compute.
- `poetry add` + commit lockfile; optional groups (`dev`, `neuro`); run via `poetry run`.
- Unit tests: BIDS paths, metadata, API contracts; integration tests for critical pipelines.

## REST API

- Resources: `datasets`, `subjects`, `sessions`, `pipelines`, `runs`, `artifacts`.
- Prefix: `/api/v1/`; consistent errors (`detail`, `code`, optional `field`).
- OpenAPI is the contract for frontend and integrators.
